    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To consume a message from a managed subscription or queue, I will use Amazon Simple Queue Service (SQS) as the concrete external provider. This choice is based on the requirement to use a managed service and the need to make the provider identifiable in the code. Amazon SQS is a widely used service for message queuing, and it provides a Python SDK (boto3) that can be used to interact with the service. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789865745382,
          "start": 1789865742541
        },
        "type": "text"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc4fd0cc001DfxoPTlbNSpCDW",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc4fcc87001pord9BIVcPagDX",
      "session_id": "ses_f43b0338dffexfisKA6b7htzMv",
