    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To create the `publish_event.py` script, I need to choose a concrete external provider for managed messaging. Amazon Simple Notification Service (SNS) is a suitable choice. I will use the Boto3 library, which is the Amazon Web Services (AWS) SDK for Python, to interact with SNS. The script will publish a JSON event to an SNS topic. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789865739413,
          "start": 1789865737240
        },
        "type": "text"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc4fbc180019ED2lbBMIu5J7t",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc4fb5e3001u8sJa56GS9nG5h",
      "session_id": "ses_f43b04aa0ffe6Vw2gLBbFcV7F7",
      "time_created": 1789865737241,
      "time_updated": 1789865739413
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "tooluse_NoGhNf6Tq6S2JeNGoo84uf",
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import boto3\nimport json\n\ndef publish_event(topic_arn, message):\n    sns_client = boto3.client('sns')\n    response = sns_client.publish(\n        TopicArn=topic_arn,\n        Message=json.dumps({'default': json.dumps(message)}),\n        MessageStructure='json'\n    )\n    return response\n\nif __name__ == '__main__'):\n    topic_arn = 'arn:aws:sns:REGION:ACCOUNT_ID:TOPIC_NAME'\n    message = {'key1': 'value1', 'key2': 'value2'}\n    response = publish_event(topic_arn, message)\n    print(response)",
            "filePath": "/private/var/folders/bf/pt_kfhl16yb4r9vfb588n1fm0000gn/T/vb-staged-mj22nljm/publish_event.py"
          },
